---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BreadcrumbJsonLd from '../../components/BreadcrumbJsonLd.astro';
import FAQPageJsonLd from '../../components/FAQPageJsonLd.astro';
import RuleQuote from '../../components/RuleQuote.astro';
import { KARNATAKA_CITIES } from '../../data/karnataka-cities';
import SectionLinks from '../../components/SectionLinks.astro';

const PAGE_URL = 'https://insurancesupport.online/karnataka/';
const TITLE = 'Insurance Claim Help in Karnataka | Hari Kotian';
const DESCRIPTION =
  'A claim refused anywhere in Karnataka goes to the insurer’s grievance officer, then Bima Bharosa, then the Ombudsman at Bengaluru — free, up to ₹50 lakh, one year to file.';
const UPDATED = '2026-11-12';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Is there an Insurance Ombudsman outside Bengaluru for Karnataka?',
    answer:
      'No. Karnataka has one Insurance Ombudsman, in Bengaluru (Jeevan Soudha building, JP Nagar 1st Phase), and its jurisdiction is the whole state. A policyholder in Mangaluru, Hubballi or Kalaburagi files with that office — by post, email or online — and does not travel unless they choose to attend a hearing.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How long do I have to complain in Karnataka?',
    answer:
      'A written complaint to the insurer comes first: it must reply within 14 days. If the reply is a refusal, or nothing arrives within a month, the Ombudsman can be approached within one year of that rejection or reply. A consumer complaint has two years.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need a lawyer for the Ombudsman?',
    answer:
      'No. The Insurance Ombudsman Rules, 2017 make no provision for engaging a lawyer, and the forum is free. That is why the paperwork matters more than the argument: a clean chronology and the rejection letter decide most cases.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you help if I am not in Bengaluru?',
    answer:
      'Yes, for the whole state — but remotely. Documents come by WhatsApp, email or post, and the grievance and Ombudsman filings are written and filed online. There is no office and no doorstep visit outside Bengaluru, and this page will not pretend otherwise.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Which consumer commission hears my case?',
    answer:
      'The District Commission where you live, up to ₹50 lakh; the State Commission at Bengaluru from ₹50 lakh to ₹2 crore; the National Commission above that. A district commission case does not require going to Bengaluru.',
  },
];

const panel = 'rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={TITLE}
  description={DESCRIPTION}
  keywords="insurance claim help Karnataka, claim rejected Karnataka, insurance ombudsman Karnataka, bima bharosa Karnataka, insurance advisor Karnataka, LIC claim Karnataka"
  canonical={PAGE_URL}
  pageType="city"
  dateModified={UPDATED}
>
  <BreadcrumbJsonLd
    items={[
      { label: 'Home', url: 'https://insurancesupport.online' },
      { label: 'Karnataka', url: PAGE_URL },
    ]}
  />
  <FAQPageJsonLd questions={faqs} />

  <main id="main" role="main">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-900 via-slate-800 to-blue-900 text-white">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 lg:py-20">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-amber-300 mb-4">Karnataka · Statewide</p>
        <h1 class="text-3xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight mb-5">Insurance claim help across Karnataka</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-200 max-w-3xl mb-4">
          <strong class="text-white">One office, in Bengaluru. One Ombudsman, also in Bengaluru, covering all 31 districts.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-300 max-w-3xl mb-4">
          If a health, motor or LIC claim has been refused, reduced or left unpaid anywhere in the state — Mysuru, Mangaluru, Hubballi, Belagavi, Kalaburagi, Ballari and everywhere between — the route is the same and the first three steps are free: written reasons from the insurer, a complaint to its Grievance Redressal Officer, then IRDAI’s Bima Bharosa, then the Insurance Ombudsman at Bengaluru.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-300 max-w-3xl mb-8">
          What changes from district to district is which consumer commission hears a case, which LIC divisional office holds the file, and how the claim usually goes wrong. Those are below, city by city.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
          <a href="/contact" class="inline-flex justify-center items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-amber-400 text-slate-900 font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-300 transition-colors">
            Send the rejection letter — first read free
          </a>
          <a href="tel:+919986634506" class="inline-flex justify-center items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-white/10 border border-white/25 text-white font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-white/20 transition-colors">
            Call +91 99866 34506
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Route -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">The route, same in every district</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-8 max-w-3xl">
        These are rules, not opinions — the timelines come from IRDAI’s Protection of Policyholders’ Interests regulations and the 5 September 2024 master circular.
      </p>
      <ol class="space-y-4">
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 mb-2">Step 1 · Ask for it in writing</p>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Get the rejection and the clause it relies on</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600">
            A refusal has to name the clause and the reason, not just say "not payable". Ask for the claim notes and the medical or survey opinion the insurer relied on; the reply is the foundation for everything that follows.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 mb-2">Step 2 · 14 days</p>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Grievance Redressal Officer of the insurer</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600">
            Every insurer must publish a GRO and answer within 14 days. This step is mandatory before any forum — skipping it is the most common reason a complaint is sent back.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 mb-2">Step 3 · Online</p>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Bima Bharosa, IRDAI’s portal</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600">
            Filed at bimabharosa.irdai.gov.in from any district. IRDAI forwards it to the insurer and the insurer answers within a fortnight. The reference number it issues is what you cite afterwards.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 mb-2">Step 4 · Within one year</p>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">The Ombudsman at Bengaluru</h3>
          <p class="text-slate-600">
            Free, no lawyer, award up to ₹50 lakh, and the insurer must pay within 30 days or ₹5,000 a day thereafter. One year from the rejection to file — the deadline people in this state most often miss.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="mt-10">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">The rule that most rejections run into</h3>
        <RuleQuote rule="noRejectionForDocuments" />
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">
          Every clock in this route is listed with its source on <a href="/insurance-claim-timelines/" class="text-blue-700 font-semibold hover:underline">the claim timelines page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Forums -->
    <section class="bg-slate-50 border-y border-slate-200">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-14">
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Which forum hears your case</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 mb-8 max-w-3xl">Two different systems, two different jobs. The Ombudsman is faster and free; the consumer commission can award compensation and has no upper limit at the national level.</p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-900">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Forum</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Sits at</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Limit</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Cost</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="text-slate-600">
              <tr class="border-t border-slate-100">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-slate-900">Insurance Ombudsman</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Bengaluru — covers all of Karnataka</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">₹50 lakh</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Free, no lawyer</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-slate-100">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-slate-900">District Commission</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Your district headquarters</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Up to ₹50 lakh</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Nominal fee</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-slate-100">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-slate-900">State Commission</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Bengaluru</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">₹50 lakh – ₹2 crore</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Fee by claim value</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-slate-100">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-slate-900">National Commission</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">New Delhi</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Above ₹2 crore</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Fee by claim value</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Cities -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">By city</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-8 max-w-3xl">
        Each page carries the district’s consumer commission, the LIC divisional office that holds the file where LIC lists one, and the failure that most often turns up there.
      </p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <a href="/bangalore/" class="group rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50 p-5 hover:border-blue-400 transition-colors">
          <p class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">Bengaluru</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">Priority city — office at Jalahalli, in-person meetings here.</p>
        </a>
        {KARNATAKA_CITIES.map((city) => (
          <a href={`/karnataka/${city.slug}/`} class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-blue-400 transition-colors">
            <p class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">
              {city.name}
              {city.former && <span class="font-normal text-slate-400"> · {city.former}</span>}
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">{city.district} district</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works remotely -->
    <section class="bg-slate-50 border-y border-slate-200">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-14">
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">How this works from outside Bengaluru</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 mb-8 max-w-3xl">
          Plainly, because most local pages on the internet are vague about it: there is one office, in Jalahalli, and no branches. Everything else is remote, and it is how these claims are actually filed anyway.
        </p>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class={panel}>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">What happens remotely</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-600 text-sm">
              <li>Documents by WhatsApp photograph, email scan or speed post.</li>
              <li>The rejection letter read, and the ground it turns on identified.</li>
              <li>The grievance drafted and sent to the insurer’s GRO by email and post.</li>
              <li>Bima Bharosa and Ombudsman filings prepared and submitted online.</li>
              <li>Written updates at each step, because phone calls leave no record.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class={panel}>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">What does not happen</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-600 text-sm">
              <li>No doorstep visit outside Bengaluru. Any page claiming otherwise is selling.</li>
              <li>No promise of a particular outcome, amount or timeline beyond the regulator’s.</li>
              <li>No filing in your name without your signature and your documents.</li>
              <li>No fee before the free first read is done and you have decided.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-slate-600 mt-8 max-w-3xl">
          If you are in Bengaluru, the same work applies and in-person meetings are possible at Jalahalli, Monday to Saturday, 9:30 am to 6 pm.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <a href="/bangalore/" class="text-blue-700 font-semibold hover:underline">The Bengaluru page →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Checklist -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">What to send, whichever district you are in</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 max-w-3xl">Photograph each of these once, clearly, and name the files so they can be found later. The first read is free and needs nothing more than this.</p>
      <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-slate-700">
        <li class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3">The rejection letter, with the date it reached you</li>
        <li class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3">The policy schedule, including any endorsements</li>
        <li class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3">The claim form you submitted, and the claim number</li>
        <li class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3">Health: discharge summary, itemised bills, prescriptions</li>
        <li class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3">Motor: FIR, survey report, repair estimate, permit and fitness</li>
        <li class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-3">LIC: premium receipts, revival letters, any correspondence</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 text-slate-600">
        More detail on what each forum wants: 
        <a href="/blog/insurance-ombudsman-bangalore-guide-2026" class="text-blue-700 hover:underline">the Ombudsman filing guide</a>, 
        <a href="/blog/irdai-bima-bharosa-complaint-filing-2026" class="text-blue-700 hover:underline">Bima Bharosa</a>, and 
        <a href="/claim-recovery/" class="text-blue-700 hover:underline">the full recovery route</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="bg-slate-50 border-t border-slate-200">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-14">
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">Karnataka questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {faqs.map((faq) => (
            <details class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5">
              <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-slate-900 list-none">{faq.question}</summary>
              <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">{faq.answer}</p>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="mt-8 text-slate-600">
          Still unsure which forum applies? <a href="/contact" class="text-blue-700 font-semibold hover:underline">Send the letter</a> and you will get a written answer on the ground it turns on.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <SectionLinks current="/karnataka/" />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
